🎬 IMDb Movie Review Sentiment Analysis using NLP & Machine Learning
📌 Project Overview

Developed an end-to-end Sentiment Analysis system to classify IMDb movie reviews as Positive 😊 or Negative 😞 using Natural Language Processing (NLP) and Machine Learning techniques. The project involved data cleaning, exploratory data analysis, feature engineering, model building, and performance evaluation to accurately predict customer sentiment from textual reviews.

📊 Dataset Information
Dataset: IMDb Movie Reviews Dataset
Total Records: 50,000 Reviews
Target Variable: Sentiment
Classes: Positive & Negative
Problem Type: Binary Text Classification
🧹 Data Cleaning & Preprocessing

To improve model performance and ensure data quality, the following preprocessing steps were performed:

✅ Removed duplicate reviews

✅ Checked and handled missing values

✅ Converted sentiment labels:

Positive → 1
Negative → 0

✅ Converted text to lowercase

✅ Removed HTML tags and special characters

✅ Removed punctuation and stopwords

✅ Performed tokenization and lemmatization

✅ Created a clean text corpus for machine learning

📈 Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA)
Key Findings

📌 Dataset contains an almost equal number of positive and negative reviews.

📌 Positive reviews frequently contained words such as:

Great
Amazing
Excellent
Best

📌 Negative reviews frequently contained words such as:

Bad
Boring
Worst
Waste
